      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T17:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should all the board-specific files have include guards to prevent accidental multiple inclusion?",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff7ce2b3_c50bff7a",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T18:25:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These files should not be included directly, since they are incomplete without the definitions in registers.h.\n\nI was thinking about putting in a check like the following, but it seemed like similar includes (config_chip.h and config-*.h) did not enforce anything.\n\n#ifndef __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H\n#error \"Chip specific register should not be included directly\"\n#endif",
      "parentUuid": "ac3fc595_f9e86f8c",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e55abf31_22aec6c7",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T18:47:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like that idea. Maybe slightly different way that would be safe against someone renaming __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H would be (in each registers file like this one):\n\n #ifndef __REGISTERS_BLAH_H\n #define __REGISTERS_BLAH_H\n\n #else\n #error \"Do not include this file directly. It is only included by the top-level registers header\"\n #endif /* __REGISTERS_BLAH_H */\n\nOr maybe invert the if statement so that the error is at the top of the file and easier to see.",
      "parentUuid": "ff7ce2b3_c50bff7a",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
