      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T19:35:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ahh, I see how that could be annoying for file renaming, but then someone could include this registers file directly without getting an error. Include both?\n\nOr, better yet, just explicitly set a different macro in registers.h that surrounds the family specific include section.\n\nSo, in registers.h:\n\n#define __REGISTERS_MASTER__\n\n#if define(FAMILY1)\n#   include \u003cregister-fam1.h\u003e\n#elif define(FAMILY2)\n#   include \u003cregister-fam2.h\u003e\n#endif\n\n#undef __REGISTERS_MASTER__\n\n\nIn registers-stm32f0.h:\n\n#ifndef __REGISTERS_FAMILY_SPECIFIC__\n#error \"\"\n#endif",
      "parentUuid": "e55abf31_22aec6c7",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5c6bc38_d862f2f1",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T19:51:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the way I suggested will work since it will generate a compile error if it gets included a second time (the \"#error\" message).",
      "parentUuid": "6a8f244c_f84a0677",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
