    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22921ab0_40bd5852",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T20:12:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that, but what are the chances that someone would include registers.h and registers-stm32f0.h, at the same time?\nAre you suggesting that it should be okay for someone to include registers-stm32f0.h directly without registers.h? Or, is this a decision of trying to reduce complexity?\n\nChecking for __REGISTERS_MASTER__ in family specific headers is pretty fool proof.\n-\u003e registers.h already has header guard\n-\u003e including a specific registers header would always be disallowed",
      "parentUuid": "e5c6bc38_d862f2f1",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed22e9ea_9bd788fb",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T21:05:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we reuse __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H (instead of adding __REGISTERS_MASTER__)?\n\nIn registers-x.h, we add:\n  #ifndef __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H\n  #error\n  #endif\n\nIn this way, registers-x.h can be included only by registers.h, right?\n\nSince registers.h is guarded by __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H for repeated inclusion, we don\u0027t need __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_X_H in registers-x.h.\n\n\u003e to include registers-stm32f0.h directly without registers.h\n\nLet\u0027s force all inclusions to be through registers.h.",
      "parentUuid": "22921ab0_40bd5852",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a911dea_773c8bf2",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T00:32:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can. To rephrase Tom\u0027s point, using that macro would inadvertently tie each of the family specific files to the registers.h file name.\nTrue, it is annoying to change tons of files, simply because you renamed a file.\nBut, I\u0027d rather that vs. a system that catches a misuse some of the time.\n\nThus, the middle ground of introducing a new non-file-name-based macro seems fitting, but I understand not wanting to introduce a new macro.",
      "parentUuid": "ed22e9ea_9bd788fb",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cf9b1d3_f7151333",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T01:43:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s unlikely registers.h will be renamed. Even if it\u0027s renamed, it\u0027ll be caught by buildall because registers-x.h will all break and replacing __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H in several files is trivial.\n\nIt\u0027s nice to have __CROS_EC_REGISTERS_H in registers-x.h because it clarifies the tie.",
      "parentUuid": "3a911dea_773c8bf2",
      "revId": "79a9192ed65d3763d16d28f795415d05b801a38e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
